Only touch symlinked gcroots when refreshing them

_nix_refresh_gcroots globs `${layout_dir}/flake-profile-*` and
`${layout_dir}/nix-profile-*`, which also match the regular
`flake-profile-<hash>.rc` / `nix-profile-<hash>.rc` cache files.
`use_flake` and `use_nix` pass those `.rc` files to `watch_file` so that
manual cache refreshes take effect. Touching them on every cache hit
rewrites their mtime, so:

  1. shell A loads the environment and records the `.rc` mtime;
  2. any other evaluation (second shell, `direnv exec`, tooling) bumps
     the `.rc` mtime;
  3. shell A's next prompt sees a changed watch file and reloads, which
     bumps the `.rc` mtime again;
  4. shell B's next prompt sees the change and reloads, and so on.

With more than one shell open this reloads on every prompt, forever.

Only the symlinks are gcroots, so restrict the touch to those and keep
the nh garbage-collection intent.

Upstream removed the whole function in 94e4fe0 ("Don't refresh
gcroots") because nh now offers `nh clean --keep-one`; this patch keeps
the refresh until that reaches a nix-direnv release.

diff --git a/direnvrc b/direnvrc
index a96152b..c37a1c4 100644
--- a/direnvrc
+++ b/direnvrc
@@ -214,12 +214,19 @@ _nix_add_gcroot() {
 _nix_refresh_gcroots() {
   # Use touch to update all symlinks' timestamps to prevent nh
   # from garbage collecting the frequently used direnv environment.
-  local layout_dir
+  #
+  # Only symlinks are gcroots. The globs also match the regular `.rc`
+  # cache files that use_flake/use_nix pass to watch_file; touching
+  # those makes every shell reload on its next prompt, which touches
+  # them again and keeps all other shells reloading forever.
+  local layout_dir f
   layout_dir=$(direnv_layout_dir)
 
-  if ! touch -h "${layout_dir}"/flake-profile-* "${layout_dir}"/flake-inputs/* "${layout_dir}"/nix-profile-* 2>/dev/null; then
-    _nix_direnv_warning "could not refresh gcroots; layout directory may be read-only"
-  fi
+  for f in "${layout_dir}"/flake-profile-* "${layout_dir}"/flake-inputs/* "${layout_dir}"/nix-profile-*; do
+    if [[ -L $f ]]; then
+      touch -h "$f"
+    fi
+  done
 }
 
 _nix_clean_old_gcroots() {
